// Package sha256 computes the SHA-256 cryptographic digest (FIPS 180-4).
//
// This is a deliberately MINIMAL, purpose-built implementation for the linker's
// Mach-O ad-hoc code-signer, which hashes each page of the output — hence its home
// in the compiler tree (pkg/binate) rather than the shared stdlib.  It is knowingly
// under-designed for a general hashing library: one-shot Sum256 only, no streaming
// Hasher (New/Write/Sum/Reset), no fixed-size Digest type, no Hash interface for
// swapping in other algorithms.  A properly-designed hashing package belongs in the
// stdlib (stdx/std) when someone builds it; keeping this one here keeps stdx clean.
package "pkg/binate/sha256"

// Sum256 returns the 32-byte SHA-256 digest of data.
func Sum256(data *[]readonly uint8) @[]uint8
